A||||18||Seanh||Did Fiero Shop ever get the hood vents done?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-03-2000||09:37 PM||||I was just wondering. I would like to know some more about them, but will probally put them on my car during the rebuild and engine swap. If so, how much are they, and where can they be found? If not, do you have any idea when they might be available?<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000001||HAGS||11-03-2000||09:54 PM||||what good do hood vents do? I can understand vents on the deck lid, but why the hood?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||11-03-2000||09:57 PM||||As I understand it the hood vents allows for better air flow through the radiator by allowing some of the air to escape out the hood vents rather than have all the air running under the car as it normally does. <P>The vents are placed in the hood behind the radiator allowing better airflow.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||11-03-2000||10:01 PM||||the proper type of hood scoops on the hood can relieve the pressure built up under the front part of the hood caused by the airflow at high speeds which can make the headlight doors flip up and down.<P>seanh, we will be producing the scoops soon!! We will also be producing a new type of side scoop as well as a front fender vent. All of these things are in the works as well as the anti bump steer kit, the brake upgrade package and the 4.9L conversions. Since we made the move into a larger shop recently it has caused a backlog of the production schedule due to the increase in traffic, both mechanical as well as parts sales......hang in there, it won't be much longer!!<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                            <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||11-03-2000||10:02 PM||||Well, I'll tell ya.  At high speeds, the effect of all that air traeling up through the front air intake can do some tricky things... front end lift, popping open of headlight doors, that kinda thing.  By allowing that air to be released over the hood provides extra downforce, not to mention reducing underhood temperatures around the radiator.  Not to mention that FieroShop's vents look really effing cool!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-03-2000||10:13 PM||||Okay, just thought I would make sure there still out there. I cant wait to get my hands on them. Have you set a price for them yet? or a ballpark figure? Thanks<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||11-03-2000||10:40 PM||||Hey TGOWENS, buy the design for the 88 steering dampner from Rodney Dickman.  He only has a few left and I don't have the money right now to buy them, he isn't making any more.  More and more people are putting 16 , 17 even 18 inch rims on and they will definitely need this.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
