Z||000008||tgowens||11-04-2000||04:20 AM||||Mike, it's liable to suck the spare outta the front end!! Seriously, is that a mustang scoop or some other type??<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                            <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000009||BOILERMAKER||11-04-2000||09:57 AM||||It's a Mustang scoop.  I originally went looking at all the big named Fiero places and those places wanted upwards of $80 (hey, if they can get people to pay those prices, more power to them).<P>Sucking the spare tire out.  LMAO.  The only opening for this scoop is right over the radiator to allow better flow.  It works too!||||reg||1
