Z||000015||Seanh||11-04-2000||07:50 PM||||I like that. I dont know about the white hood on a red car, but that scoop idea is cool. I might have to do somthing like that on my project car once mine is done. I think Fiero Shops are going to be the best looking all around. I also love Archies too. I like all three. Maybe I will have to buy some more Fieros and try one of each.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">   <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>If you smoke after sex, your doing it way to fast.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000016||rockcrawl||11-04-2000||08:08 PM||||Here's a not-so-great pic of my 87 GT ricer. The scoop is a 69 Camaro cowl induction style, glassed in. The area of the hood was cut out above the radiator to allow heat and pressure to get <B>out</B>. The cowl induction style is designed to take advantage of the high pressure area at the base of the windsheild to help draw air <B>in</B>. I'm not sure if this is a good scoop for a Fiero. At best it will have little or no effect. At worst, it will create more unwanted high pressure under the hood. But it sure does look cool! The Fiero Shop's and Archie's vents are far more functional.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87gt_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000017||2xsess||11-04-2000||08:39 PM||||Ok, I have to ask......<BR>What's up with the Corvette emblem on your GT Rockcrawl?????<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||rockcrawl||11-05-2000||05:55 PM||||Oh, I don't know. I had a Corvette emblem laying around, so I decided to cut the center out so it would fit over the Fiero emblem. At the time, I thought it looked cool, but I wouldn't do it again! I was just going through a rice-boy stage I guess! I figured if my car had a Vette part on it, it would go faster! I sold the car that way, and as far as I know, it's still on there.||||reg||1
